ossibly be on that debate  stage no one of color there would be  more billionaires than the race than  black people is that a problem to you  Cory Booker endorsed me a number of  times and I endorsed Cory Booker number  times he's very well-spoken he's got  some good ideas it would be better the  more diverse any group is but the public  is out there picking and choosing and  rowing down this field the truth of the  matter is you had a lot of diversity in  the candidates some of whom were very  competent why they aren't there as you  narrowed it down you have to talk to  other people who are experts I don't  know part of the conversation is here we  go another old white gentleman isn't it  time for change isn't it time for  somebody maybe but lots of people can  enter there was no reason if you wanted  to enter and run for president nine  states you could have done that but  don't complain to me that you're not in  the race it was up to you and I thought  there was a lot of diversity in the  group of democratic aspirants entry is  not a barrier so you're saying if you  want diversity then get in that is  exactly a good place to phrase it thank  you very much Mayor Bloomberg was really  he had a lot to say about a lot of  different issues but he clearly is up  for the fight he knows it's going to be  a fight he knows it's not going to be  easy and he really said I've been doing  a lot of thinking because I really  hadn't intended to run but he's so  distressed and so disturbed by what he  sees happening in Washington that he  does think he can make a difference  polling at 5% in one poll which is  considering how ladies enter to the  races is a is a strong number but and  then he told me he plans to go to every  single state before the election because  I said you know how are people going to  get to know you he goes well I'm talking  to you right now I'll be doing  interviews we have campaign ads but he  intends to go to every single state  before ya know we'll see 